            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis should already be possible by using [`paste`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e623d29561746637b49d30d6434338f88f44e856/doc/mini-pick.txt#L712) mapping when picker is active. It can paste text [from any register](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e623d29561746637b49d30d6434338f88f44e856/doc/mini-pick.txt#L526). In this particular case, typing `<C-r>+` (or `<C-r>*` depending on which selection register you use) should work as intended.\r\n\r\nThat said, making pasting using terminal shortcut was on my \"see if this is possible\" to-do list, so I'll take a look at it somewhat later.",
