        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I tried both\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufEnter\", {\n    callback = function(args)\n      if require(\"mini.pick\").is_picker_active() then\n        vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<d-v>\", \"<c-r>+\", { buffer = args.buf, noremap = true, silent = true })\n        vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufLeave\", {\n          buffer = args.buf,\n          callback = function() vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<d-v>\", '\"+p', { noremap = true, silent = true }) end,\n          once = true,\n        })\n      end\n    end,\n  })\n```\n\nand\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"FileType\", {\n    pattern = \"MiniPick\",\n    callback = function(args)\n      vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<d-v>\", \"<c-r>+\", { buffer = args.buf, noremap = true, silent = true })\n      vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"BufLeave\", {\n        buffer = args.buf,\n        callback = function() vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<d-v>\", '\"+p', { noremap = true, silent = true }) end,\n        once = true,\n      })\n    end,\n  })\n```\n\nBut didn't have luck. `<c-r>+` is sufficient, but it would be nice to use the same paste command within the pickers.",
