        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I did it a bit differently. This way, it's like an alias for `<C-r>+`, avoiding some issues I had, such as interpreting the pasted text as a character and clearing the search bar when I try to paste again.\n\n```lua\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup({\n\toptions = { use_cache = true },\n\twindow = { config = win_config },\n\tmappings = {\n\t\tchoose_in_vsplit = \"<C-CR>\",\n\t\tsys_paste = {\n\t\t\tchar = \"<C-v>\",\n\t\t\tfunc = function()\n\t\t\t\tvim.api.nvim_feedkeys(vim.api.nvim_replace_termcodes(\"<C-r>+\", true, true, true), \"n\", true)\n\t\t\tend,\n\t\t},\n\t},\n})\n```",
